.TH STRTOF 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
strtof \- parse an ASCII floating-point value as binary32
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdlib.h>
.PP
.BI "float strtof(const char* " text ", char** " end ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uses the input grammar and end-pointer rules of
.BR strtod (3crunch),
but rounds directly to binary32, without an intermediate binary64 rounding.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the nearest binary32 value, ties to even, independent of the
floating-point environment. No conversion returns positive zero.
Overflow returns signed infinity and sets
.B errno
to
.BR ERANGE .
An inexact result rounded to a subnormal or zero also sets
.BR ERANGE .
Other results leave
.B errno
unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR strtod (3crunch),
.BR strtold (3crunch)
